From b895b90c9d192f0f90defba491a8c2a6024103b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Michael <22668877+arraypress@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:49:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Parse Swift 6 syntax: sending, isolated, copy, value
 generics, inline arrays, and more

- `sending` and `isolated` parameter modifiers (SE-0430, SE-0313), `-> sending T` results, and
  `isolated deinit` (SE-0371)
- `copy x` (SE-0377), beside `consume x`
- Value generics `<let rows: Int>` and integer type arguments `InlineArray<4, Int>` (SE-0452)
- Inline array sugar `[3 of Int]` (SE-0483)
- Freestanding macros with no arguments, such as `#isolation` as a default value
- Labeled version arguments in attributes: `@backDeployed(before: macOS 14)`
- Optional of a bracket-qualified type: `[Int].Index?`
- A multiline extended regex whose closing `/#` is indented

The new keywords stay contextual: `let sending = 1`, `let copy = 3` still parse.
New corpus: test/corpus/swift6.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 grammar.js             |  53 +++++++--
 test/corpus/swift6.txt | 260 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 304 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
